<.shell title="Activity panel" current={:activity_panel}>
  <h1>Activity panel</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    An activity at a glance: its day and time, the counts, your reply, and Take attendance.
  </p>

  <div class="demo">
    <.activity_panel
      id="activity-panel-demo"
      activity={panel_activity()}
      team={sample_team()}
      now={panel_now()}
      counts={panel_counts()}
      team_admin?={true}
    >
      <:reply><.reply id="activity-panel-demo-reply" state={:yes} /></:reply>
    </.activity_panel>
  </div>

  <h3>As Next up</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <.activity_panel
      id="activity-panel-next-up-demo"
      label="Next up"
      activity={panel_activity()}
      team={sample_team()}
      now={panel_now()}
    >
      <.activity_kind_mark activity={panel_activity()} class="text-sm" />
      <h2 class="activity-panel-title"><a href="#" class="link">Rope rescue, Murrin Park</a></h2>
      <p class="hint">Murrin Park · in 3 hours · 6 signed up</p>
      <:reply><.reply id="activity-panel-next-up-demo-reply" state={:ask} /></:reply>
    </.activity_panel>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Under an activity's title, for everyone.</li>
    <li>
      On the Dashboard as Next up, the team's next activity, with its title and place. Its count
      goes in the place's line, "Murrin Park · in 3 hours · 6 signed up", not a line of its own.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>
    A list of activities. Each gets a row, such as Coming up's, or a <a href={page_path(:table)}>table</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The day and time come first, in large type: "Today", "Tomorrow", then "Thu Oct 29".</li>
    <li>
      The counts read "6 signed up · 2 can't make it · 5 no reply", then "6 attended · 2 absent · 5 no reply" once it starts. A zero is left out, except the first.
    </li>
    <li>
      A member it invites gets their <a href={page_path(:reply)}>reply</a>
      under the counts, until it starts. Anyone else gets the counts alone.
    </li>
    <li>
      Team admins get Take attendance, the page's primary button, in every state. Members get no
      button.
    </li>
    <li>
      On a phone it stacks: the day and time on one line, then the rest, then a full-width button.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.activity_panel id="…" activity=&#123;…&#125; team=&#123;…&#125; now=&#123;…&#125; counts=&#123;…&#125; team_admin?=&#123;…&#125;&gt;</code>
    with the reply control in its <code>&lt;:reply&gt;</code>
    slot. Next up adds <code>label="Next up"</code>
    and its title and place inside, and leaves out <code>counts</code>.
  </p>
</.shell>
